@* Main menu. Two routes into the same three-step order wizard, differing only in where the
   order lives between pages. Everything else — the fields, the steps, the layout — is held
   constant so that the one variable under study is the storage. *@
@page "/"

<PageTitle>Day 3 — Two Paths</PageTitle>

<h1>Two paths through the same order</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Both paths collect the same three pieces of information across three steps, and both let you
    edit the <strong>quantity</strong> on every step. The only difference is where the data lives
    between pages.
</p>

<div class="row mt-4">
    <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
        <div class="card h-100 border-danger">
            <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
                <h5 class="card-title">Path 1 — No Store</h5>
                <p class="card-text">
                    The order is hand-carried from page to page in the <strong>address bar</strong>.
                    The wizard buttons pass it along. The browser's Back and Forward buttons do not —
                    they replay an older URL that holds an older copy of the order.
                </p>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    <small>Watch the address bar. The object is sitting in it.</small>
                </p>
                <a class="btn btn-danger mt-auto" href="classic/step1">Start Path 1 &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
        <div class="card h-100 border-success">
            <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
                <h5 class="card-title">Path 2 — Flux Store</h5>
                <p class="card-text">
                    The order lives in a single <strong>store</strong> outside every page. The URLs
                    carry nothing. Wizard buttons, Back, Forward — every page reads the same one
                    copy, so there is nothing to drift out of sync.
                </p>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    <small>Watch the address bar here too. It stays empty.</small>
                </p>
                <a class="btn btn-success mt-auto" href="flux/step1">Start Path 2 &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-secondary mt-3">
    <strong>Try this on both paths:</strong> change the quantity on step 2, then press the
    browser's <strong>Back</strong> button and the <strong>Forward</strong> button instead of the
    wizard buttons. One path keeps your edit. The other does not.
</div>
